{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Leo, thanks for reaching out. I can't install Zoom directly, but you may be able to add it yourself. Please open Company Portal (Software Center) on your laptop and search for Zoom. If it's listed, install it from there. If it isn't listed, reply to this ticket with your manager's approval, since apps outside the Company Portal need manager approval and a security review before we can install them. Once approved, we'll get it installed. If you need it before tomorrow's meeting, let us know the meeting time so we can prioritize it. You can also join the meeting from a browser if Zoom isn't ready in time.",
  "internal_note": "Sender: Leo Martins (user_id 6), Sales, Account Executive, device BL-LT-0106, account active, no lockouts. Request: install Zoom client for client meeting tomorrow. Per KB-027, first step is to check whether Zoom is in Company Portal; I cannot view the portal, so the user was asked to check it. If not in the portal, the request needs manager approval plus security review of the app. No install was attempted and no admin rights or install links were provided. Escalate to Tier 2 with app name, version, business reason, and approver once the manager approves and Zoom is not in the portal. Note the client meeting is tomorrow, so ask for a timeline.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-027"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
